evidence_verified":true,"key":"population","score":30},{"assessment":"Shifts the legal burden of proof to the government by clear and convincing evidence and mandates expedited hearings and attorney fee awards for successful complainants.","evidence":"the respondent shall bear the burden of proving by clear and convincing evidence that the individual is ineligible to receive or possess a firearm.","evidence_verified":true,"key":"magnitude","score":50},{"assessment":"Requires the government to pay reasonable attorney fees and litigation costs in successful cases, but specifies no overall dollar cost or appropriation.","evidence":"The court shall assess against the respondent reasonable attorney fees and other litigation costs reasonably incurred","evidence_verified":true,"key":"fiscal","score":20},{"assessment":"Amends federal law regarding judicial remedies, court hearing timelines, and annual reporting requirements for the FBI.","evidence":"The court shall hold a hearing on an action brought under subsection (a), within 30 days after the action is brought.","evidence_verified":true,"key":"scope","score":40},{"assessment":"Creates permanent statutory procedural rules and ongoing annual reporting requirements for the FBI.","evidence":"The Director of the Federal Bureau of Investigation shall submit annually to the Committee on the Judiciary of the House of Representatives and the Committee on the Judiciary of the Senate a written report","evidence_verified":true,"key":"duration","score":70}],"missing_information":["Estimated number of individuals affected annually by delays over 60 days."],"rationale":"The bill expands judicial remedies and procedural rules for individuals experiencing extended delays over 60 days on firearm transfers through the National Instant Criminal Background Check System.","score":40},"importance_meta":{"generated_at":"2026-10-26T22:43:45+00:00","model":"gemini-3.5-flash-lite","source_basis":"text+summary","source_urls":["https://www.congress